  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    for r1 in range(rows):\n        for c1 in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r1][c1]\n            # Extend to find the right edge of potential top border\n            for c2 in range(c1 + 2, cols):\n                if grid[r1][c2] != v:\n                    break\n                # Now look for the bottom border at row r2\n                for r2 in range(r1 + 2, rows):\n                    # Quick check on corners of bottom edge\n                    if grid[r2][c1] != v or grid[r2][c2] != v:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Verify bottom edge is all v\n                    valid = True\n                    for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                        if grid[r2][c] != v:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Verify left edge is all v\n                    for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                        if grid[r][c1] != v:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Verify right edge is all v\n                    for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                        if grid[r][c2] != v:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Extract interior\n                    interior = []\n                    for r in range(r1 + 1, r2):\n                        interior.append(grid[r][c1 + 1:c2])\n                    return interior\n    \n    return []\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    for r1 in range(rows):\n        for c1 in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r1][c1]\n            # Extend to find the right edge of potential top border\n            for c2 in range(c1 + 2, cols):\n                if grid[r1][c2] != v:\n                    break\n                # Now look for the bottom border at row r2\n                for r2 in range(r1 + 2, rows):\n                    # Quick check on corners of bottom edge\n                    if grid[r2][c1] != v or grid[r2][c2] != v:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Verify bottom edge is all v\n                    valid = True\n                    for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                        if grid[r2][c] != v:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Verify left edge is all v\n                    for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                        if grid[r][c1] != v:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Verify right edge is all v\n                    for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                        if grid[r][c2] != v:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    \n                    # Extract interior\n                    interior = []\n                    for r in range(r1 + 1, r2):\n                        interior.append(grid[r][c1 + 1:c2])\n                    return interior\n    \n    return []",
